  "paragraphs": [
    [
      "P001",
      "ASSEMBLING PUMP SET",
      false,
      "heading",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P002",
      "Ø330/415/418/465/525",
      false,
      "heading",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P003",
      "1. Lead the water deflector (11) over the shaft until\nit touches the cover under bearing (26) and then\nfurther 1-1.5 mm towards the cover under\nbearing.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001",
        "S002"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P004",
      "2. Assemble bearing cover and rear cover.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001",
        "S002"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P005",
      "Do not\nfasten bearing cover and electric motor until the\nmotor has been mounted and the shaft can\nrotate freely without.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001",
        "S002"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P006",
      "10.3.4. Fitting shaft seal",
      false,
      "heading",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001",
        "S002"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P007",
      "For pumps with balanced shaft seal type ELK (=”-L” included in pump code on name plate) please\nread appendix A.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001",
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P008",
      "1. Clean the recess in the rear cover.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001",
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P009",
      "2. Remove the protective coating of the seat\nwithout scratching the lapped surface and\nlubricate the outer rubber L-ring on the seat with\na thin layer of silicone grease.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001",
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P010",
      "Use a brush and\nensure that no silicone grease ends up at the\nslide surface.",
      false,
      "prose",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001",
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P011",
      "DESMI Pumping Technology A/S\nTagholm 1",
      false,
      "prose",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001",
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P012",
      "9400 Nørresundby – Denmark\nTlf. nr.: +45 96 32 81 11\nFax +45 98 17 54 99\n106\nE-mail: desmi@desmi.com www.desmi.com",
      false,
      "prose",
      "107:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S001",
        "S003"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P013",
      "ASSEMBLING PUMP SET",
      true,
      "heading",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      []
    ],
    [
      "P014",
      "3. Press the seat into place with the fingers and\ncheck that all parts are correctly imbedded.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P015",
      "NOTE: If it is necessary to use tools for assembling, then protect the sliding surface of the\nseat to prevent it from being scratched or cut.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P016",
      "Lubricate the inner surface of the slide ring\nrubber bellows with a thin layer of silicone grease (ensure that no silicone grease ends up at\nthe slide surfaces) and push it over the shaft.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P017",
      "The use of a conical fitting bush as shown on\nthe assembly drawing is recommended to avoid that the rubber bellows is cut.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P018",
      "NOTE: Push the slide ring over the shaft with the hand.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P019",
      "If the rubber bellows is tight, use a\nfitting tool and take care that the slide ring is not damaged.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P020",
      "If the carbon ring is not fixed, it is\nimportant to check that it is fitted correctly, i.e. the chamfered/lapped side is to face the seat.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P021",
      "The carbon ring can be held by a little grease.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P022",
      "NOTE: When using silicone grease on the shaft, the bellows will settle and seat in abt. 15\nminutes, and until then tightness should not be expected.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P023",
      "After start, check by viewing the\nleak hole that there are no leaks.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P024",
      "10.3.5. Fitting impeller",
      true,
      "heading",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P025",
      "Ø215/265",
      true,
      "heading",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004",
        "S005"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P026",
      "1. Fit the sunk key in the shaft and lead the\nimpeller towards the shoulder of the shaft.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004",
        "S005",
        "S006"
      ]
    ],
    [
      "P027",
      "Secure the impeller with washers (7 and 8) and\na nut.",
      true,
      "prose",
      "108:column:0",
      null,
      [
        "S004",
        "S005",
        "S006"
      ]
    ],
    [
